                    {
                        "sense_id": "c5abc634-a850-3acf-b6f5-5f49e0f97565",
                        "entry_id": "726d492a-6904-35ea-8a7e-ca950e7c5ad2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to curse, to damn"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "imperfective"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "76b81387-6d89-4429-b075-78f3841458dc",
                                "sense_id": "c5abc634-a850-3acf-b6f5-5f49e0f97565",
                                "text": "Е́сли им дать, то они́ ещё попро́сят; а отказа́ть — бу́дут клясть, спле́тничать, жела́ть вся́ких напа́стей.",
                                "translation": "If you give them, they will ask for more; but if you refuse – they will curse you, gossip, and wish you all sorts of misfortunes.",
                                "english": "If you give them, they will ask for more; but if you refuse – they will curse you, gossip, and wish you all sorts of misfortunes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
